                  {
                    "t": "Composed in 1999 for the PC demo “Great Hirmu Sisters” but released as a C64 executable only in 2021."
                  }
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "quote",
              "by": "Deetsay",
              "role": "composer",
              "paragraphs": [
                [
                  {
                    "t": "[…] this was actually a pretty big project consisting of:"
                  }
                ],
                [
                  {
                    "t": "1) Hunting down the "
                  },
                  {
                    "t": "three",
                    "em": true
                  },
                  {
                    "t": " original randomly named DMC5 tunes from the floppy disks whereupon they were saved 22 years ago;"
                  }
                ],
                [
                  {
                    "t": "2) Figuring out how to integrate the SAM speech between them (massive thanks to Groepaz for releasing the commented disassembly!);"
                  }
                ],
                [
                  {
                    "t": "3) Coding a bunch of changing parameters on the DMC tunes, which were originally tweaked while recording"
                  }
                ]
              ]
            }
          ],
